    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 9ed0d99171660de538e44b07ff1d7555f6deaf10 -->\n**Review (M3, safety tier): needs one pinning test before merge.** The code itself is right.\n\n**What looks good:**\n- Probe and plasma are judged on a reduced-fidelity model by the #864 rule: a tolerance gives the model's excess back while some positive tolerance is left. Past that, the program gate refuses by name.\n- A full-fidelity model (excess = 0) behaves as before.\n- The cone and engrave rides and the cross drill stay refused, with stated reasons (`Refs #1053`).\n- No unwrap or panic, and no goldens, snapshots, process files or dependencies touched.\n\n**Local results** (trial-merged with main):\n- motion lib 212;\n- app: `coarse_laws` 6, `coarse_probe_plasma` 7, `plasma_post` 5, `plasma_gate` 6, `plasma_profile` 7, `probe_op` 12, `probe_reach` 5, `probe_search` 3, `model_fidelity` 9, `coarse_contain` 1, `tool_body_drill_probe` 5, `refusal_ghost` 4, the `golden_cl` plasma plate;\n- clippy is clean.\n\n**Mutation checks:** reverting any of these fails a pin:\n- the probe slack;\n- `kerf_tol`;\n- the reach-law slack;\n- the kerf-law offset;\n- `excess_aware` for probe or for plasma.\n\n**Requested before merge**\n1. **The cover law's excess is not pinned.** If `cover_law` gets plain `KERF_TOL` instead of `p.kerf_tol()` (`crates/motion/src/plasma/emit.rs:284`, `laws.rs` ~78), every test stays green. So the cover law could silently loosen on a coarse model, which the PR and the decision file claim cannot happen. Please add a test with an edge between `kerf + KERF_TOL - excess` and `kerf + KERF_TOL` that is refused only on the coarse model.\n\n**Merge-time refresh hunks:**\n- `fidelity_law.rs`, the `excess_aware` doc and match arm: keep `Section::Plasma => true`, plus main's `Section::WireEdm | Section::Sinker => false`.\n- `tests/coarse_laws.rs`, the `refused` list: keep main's `WireContour, SinkerBurn`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
