    "body": "Review fix (M3) pushed at 961ed09d, for the item at 9ed0d991.\n- `plasma/emit.rs` `cut()` now reads `p.kerf_tol()` once and passes that same `tol` to the kerf law's forbidden band and to the cover law's reach, so neither can fall back to plain `KERF_TOL` on its own.\n- New pin `plasma::tests::the_cover_law_reads_the_tightened_tolerance_on_a_coarse_model`: the plate's judged top edge sits between the two reaches, so it is covered at full fidelity and refused by name on a coarse model.\n- Mutations: `cover_law` reading plain `KERF_TOL` fails the new pin, and `tol = KERF_TOL` in `cut()` fails `coarse_probe_plasma::a_kerf_between_the_tolerances_is_refused_only_on_the_coarse_model`.\n- Results: motion plasma tests 17 pass, and `coarse_probe_plasma` passes (7 tests). Clippy on motion is clean.\n- Main is not merged in yet (the conflicts are refreshed at merge time). M5 re-reviews this; `needs-rework` is left for the reviewer.",
