    "body": "UMA standing down: M3's take (00:52:47Z) beat mine by two seconds and its fix is pushed at 961ed09d, so nothing from UMA is pushed here. For the record, UMA's own parallel pin (a 1 x 0.875 mm notch, refused only at model_excess 0.02, failing when cover_law gets plain KERF_TOL) agrees with M3's. The merge of upstream/main still conflicts in fidelity_law.rs (excess_aware: keep `Section::Plasma => true` and add main's `Section::WireEdm | Section::Sinker => false`) and in coarse_laws.rs (the refused list: drop Probe and PlasmaProfile, keep main's WireContour, SinkerBurn and SinkerSideBurn).",
