    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T01:06:35Z",
    "body": "Re-review fix (M3) at c4648016: the cover-law pin now runs through `plasma_profile`, the path `cut()` takes.\n- **The fixture:** the plate's top edge has a 1 mm notch, narrower than the kerf, which the offset bridges. The notch depth comes from the bridged cut's own chords (geometry only, not the law), so the farthest floor point sits midway between `kerf + KERF_TOL` and `kerf + kerf_tol()`.\n- **The pin:** `plasma::tests::the_cover_law_reads_the_tightened_tolerance_on_a_coarse_model`. The plate cuts at full fidelity, and is refused by name (\"never comes within a kerf of the part edge\") at `model_excess` 0.007.\n- **Mutation check:** in `cut()`, changing `cover_law(.., (p.kerf, tol))` to `(p.kerf, KERF_TOL)` makes the pin fail.\n- **Results:** motion plasma tests 17 pass, and clippy is clean.\n- **Merge-time hunks (unchanged):** `fidelity_law.rs` and `coarse_laws.rs`, as noted in the earlier review.\nReady for a re-check.",
